text:
maria-seng: Quick heads-up — SilverCrest POC kickoff in 30m. They want streaming responses + tool/function calling for live lookups, and strict structured JSON output that maps to their transaction schema. Also asked about pricing for dedicated capacity and SSO/IP allowlist blockers.

 tom-se: Ack. Who's owning the schema mapping? Any sample JSON from them?

maria-seng: They dropped a sample CSV and a proto earlier, but not the final JSON mapping. I'll paste the sample after the call. Main ask: when the model returns items, they want each token-chunk to stream but still keep the final structured payload validated against their schema.

anika-presales: For streaming + structured output we typically recommend function/tool-calling pattern so the model emits a single function call with the JSON body at the end. That way you get streaming text for user experience and a deterministic structured payload once the call completes.

tom-se: Agreed. Implementation note: use the SDK streaming websocket or SSE for chunked text; buffer until function call payload arrives. Example flow: 1) stream tokens for UI, 2) on function_call event, stop streaming UI and parse the args as JSON, 3) run schema validation server-side.

maria-seng: Can you drop a short Node snippet we can share with their engineers? They prefer JS.

anika-presales: Sure — minimal example:```js
const stream = await client.stream.chat.completions.create({
  model: 'redwood/gpt-stream-1',
  messages,
  functions: [{ name: 'emit_transaction', parameters: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, amount: { type: 'number' }}, required: ['id','amount']}}],
  stream: true
});
stream.on('event', (e) => {
  if (e.type === 'response.delta') ui.append(e.delta);
  if (e.type === 'response.function_call') {
    const payload = JSON.parse(e.function_call.arguments);
    validateAgainstSchema(payload);
  }
});
```

tom-se: That's perfect. Note for them: if you need KV / prefix caching with streaming, set ephemeral cache keys per session — saves tokens.

maria-seng: Security Qs: They require SAML SSO + IP allowlist and want to run an instance in VPC eventually. Any blockers on our side for the POC?

anika-presales: For the POC we can do hosted with IP allowlist + short-lived API keys for their engineers. SAML-backed SSO needs the Private plan (or enterprise setup) — we can demo SSO via a test tenant but production IS/IT will want Private or Dedicated.

tom-se: For IP allowlist during POC, they need a static egress NAT from their side to add to our allowlist, or we can put the demo in their VPC if they want full isolation — that requires Dedicated onboarding time (2–3 weeks).

maria-seng: Pricing note: they asked for ballpark dedicated monthly commit for 4x A100-equivalent nodes. Any quick numbers?

anika-presales: Ballpark: $XXk–$YYk/month depending on retention and burst. I'll get a proper estimate from finance and attach. For POC we can offer a short-term trial credit on hosted to validate integration before they commit.

tom-se: Also flagging telemetry: they'll want per-request latency + token costs exposed in telemetry. Recommend adding route-level tracing headers now so we can map POC requests to sample traces.

maria-seng: Good call. I'll request the schema and their SAML metadata in the kickoff. Can someone prepare a one-page runbook for the engineers: 1) quick SDK example, 2) streaming->function_call flow, 3) IP allowlist steps, 4) expected timelines for Dedicated.

anika-presales: I'll draft the runbook and the pricing stub, share in 2 hours.

deploy-bot: Reminder: onboarding checklist for Dedicated requires: signed SLA, infra whitepaper, SSO metadata, and billing PO.

tom-se: Thanks — I'll prep the trace headers snippet and a small validation lambda they can drop into their pipeline.

maria-seng: Awesome. If we don't get the final schema in 24h, we'll use the CSV to mock JSON and proceed. :thumbsup:
